      "statements": {
        "f1": "The maintenance tracking API primary host is mrw-kestrel-track.invalid. The work-package planner uses it to retrieve open task cards.",
        "f2": "On 2026-03-12, the maintenance tracking API primary host changed to mrw-vireo-track.invalid after the previous host developed intermittent connection failures.",
        "d": "The maintenance tracking API returns task-card status and signoff timestamps. Clients should use the service health endpoint before starting a bulk reconciliation."
      },
      "query": "What is the current primary host for the maintenance tracking API?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t02",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The parts and rotables inventory archive bucket is mrw-dune-crate-parts. It holds closed movement records for reconciliation.",
        "f2": "On 2026-04-09, the parts and rotables inventory archive bucket changed to mrw-birch-dock-parts so the archive could use the revised lifecycle policy.",
        "d": "The parts and rotables inventory records serial-number movements separately from quantity-only consumables. Archive jobs run after the daily ledger close."
      },
      "query": "Which archive bucket does the parts and rotables inventory currently use?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t03",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The engine health feed ingestion queue is mrw-heron-core-q. Feed workers consume vibration and temperature samples from it.",
        "f2": "On 2026-05-18, the engine health feed ingestion queue changed to mrw-jasper-exhaust-q to isolate sample processing from a congested worker pool.",
        "d": "The engine health feed rejects samples without an engine identifier or capture timestamp. Rejected samples remain available for investigation."
      },
      "query": "What is the current ingestion queue for the engine health feed?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t04",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The hangar tool kiosks daily sync time is 05:20 UTC / mrw-eaststand. The sync reconciles checkouts before the morning tool count.",
        "f2": "On 2026-02-24, the hangar tool kiosks daily sync time changed to 02:25 UTC / mrw-bayline to avoid contention with the shift-start kiosk checks.",
        "d": "Hangar tool kiosks retain checkout events locally during a network interruption. Supervisors review any unmatched returns after connectivity resumes."
      },
      "query": "What is the current daily sync time for the hangar tool kiosks?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t05",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The technical records renderer deployed version is mrw-rec-7.1.5. It produces the signed PDF copies attached to closed work packages.",
        "f2": "On 2026-06-03, the technical records renderer deployed version changed to mrw-rec-8.3.7 to correct page ordering in multi-aircraft exports.",
        "d": "The technical records renderer preserves the source record identifiers in its output. Records staff compare a sample against the originals after each deployment."
      },
      "query": "Which version of the technical records renderer is currently deployed?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t06",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The work-package planner dispatch tool is mrw-LanternFlow. Planners use it to hand approved packages to hangar coordinators.",
        "f2": "On 2026-07-14, the work-package planner dispatch tool changed to mrw-SlateRunner because the previous tool could not reliably retry delayed handoffs.",
        "d": "The work-package planner keeps draft assignments separate from approved dispatches. A coordinator can see the approval history on each package."
      },
      "query": "What dispatch tool does the work-package planner currently use?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t07",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The torque wrench calibration advance expiry warning threshold is 23 days / mrw-zyphorax. Tool-control staff use the warning to schedule replacements.",
        "f2": "On 2026-08-05, the torque wrench calibration advance expiry warning threshold changed to 47 days / mrw-xelquinn after the calibration lab extended its booking lead time.",
        "d": "Torque wrench calibration records are linked to each tool's asset tag. A wrench with an expired certificate cannot be issued at a kiosk."
      },
      "query": "What is the current advance expiry warning threshold for torque wrench calibration?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t08",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The airworthiness directive ledger audit snapshot retention is 96 months / mrw-iris. The snapshots preserve the state used for periodic audit reviews.",
        "f2": "On 2026-04-27, the airworthiness directive ledger audit snapshot retention changed to 72 months / mrw-gannet after records staff approved a revised retention schedule.",
        "d": "The airworthiness directive ledger links applicability decisions to the aircraft and engine records considered. Reviewers can inspect who approved each decision."
      },
      "query": "What is the current audit snapshot retention for the airworthiness directive ledger?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t09",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The component quarantine alerts notification channel is #mrw-saffron-alerts. Inventory supervisors watch it for newly blocked serial numbers.",
        "f2": "On 2026-09-11, the component quarantine alerts notification channel changed to #mrw-flint-alerts to give quarantine notices a dedicated response rota.",
        "d": "Component quarantine alerts include the affected serial number and the reason for the hold. Clearing a hold requires an inventory supervisor's recorded approval."
      },
      "query": "Which notification channel currently receives component quarantine alerts?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t10",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The engine trend review dashboard is mrw-vibraze-board. Reliability engineers use it to compare recent readings with each engine's baseline.",
        "f2": "On 2026-10-06, the engine trend review dashboard changed to mrw-spindrift-board because the previous view omitted late-arriving samples.",
        "d": "Engine trend review takes place after the overnight feed reconciliation. Analysts annotate unusual readings before escalating them to maintenance planning."
      },
      "query": "What dashboard is currently used for engine trend review?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t11",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The brake wear scan nightly export bucket is mrw-falcon-brake-export. The export contains measurements awaiting reliability analysis.",
        "d": "Brake wear scan results are checked for missing wheel positions before the nightly export. Incomplete scans remain visible to the inspection team."
      },
      "query": "Which bucket receives the brake wear scan nightly export?"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrw.t12",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The engine borescope images storage region is mrw-zone-bracken-2. Image records carry the inspection date and engine serial number.",
        "d": "Engine borescope images are associated with the corresponding inspection task card. Reviewers can compare a new image with prior inspections."
      },
      "query": "What is the storage region for engine borescope images?"
